The dashed curve is $y=x^{2}$ and the solid curve is its translation. Which equation matches the solid curve?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.6,0)--(2.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.9)--(0,3.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-1.78:1.78,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.24:2.24,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x-2});
\node[gray,right] at (1.5,2.9) {$y=x^{2}$};
\fill[gray] (0,0) circle (2pt);
\fill (0,-2) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$(0,-2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The dashed curve is $y=x^{2}$ and the solid curve is its translation. Which translation produces the solid curve?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.6,0)--(2.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.7)--(0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,gray,dashed,<->,domain=-1.78:1.78,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x});
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.48:1.48,smooth,samples=51,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x+2});
\node[gray,right] at (1.5,2.6) {$y=x^{2}$};
\fill[gray] (0,0) circle (2pt);
\fill (0,2) circle (2pt) node[right] {$(0,2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
